 ## Queue and Tickets
 
+### Queue
+
+A **queue** belongs to one entity and holds that entity's tickets. Attributes:
+
+- `name`, `slug` (unique within the entity), `is_active` (default true),
+  optional `labels_i18n` (JSON, locale-specific labels).
+- Issuance into an **inactive** queue is rejected (`InactiveQueueException`);
+  the active flag is re-read from the database inside the issuance transaction
+  (row lock), so a queue deactivated after the caller loaded it is still
+  rejected and nothing is persisted.
+
 ### Ticket
 
-Unit of service in the queue. It is **single-use** and receives **one single call** — all data is immutable after issuance, except `called_at` and `called_by` (filled when called). Attributes:
+Unit of service in the queue. It is **single-use** and receives **one single call**:
 
 - Source queue — the ticket belongs to **one** queue (within the entity); does not record which totem it came from.
-- Priority (numeric, see below).
-- Issuance timestamp (ordering "oldest first" within same priority).
-- Issuance channel: totem, virtual, printed copy, etc.
+- Display `code`: per-queue sequence `A001`, `A002`, … (prefix `A`, at least 3
+  zero-padded digits; beyond 999 it grows: `A1000`, `A1001`, …). Unique per
+  `(queue_id, code)`. The next code is "last valid code + 1" by insertion
+  order — deleting a ticket never reuses its number; malformed legacy codes
+  (anything not matching `A<digits>`) are skipped when computing the next code.
+- Priority (numeric, see below; `>= 0`, default 0; negative is rejected with
+  `InvalidArgumentException`).
+- Issuance channel: `totem`, `virtual` (default), `printed`.
+- Status: `waiting` (initial) → `called`. There is **no cancelled status**.
+- `issued_at` (set at issuance), plus call fields `called_at` and
+  `called_by_user_id` (nullable FK to users) filled at call time.
+- Concurrent issuance retries a few times on a `(queue_id, code)` collision.
+
+### Write-once and calling
+
+All ticket fields are immutable after issuance, **except** `status`,
+`called_at` and `called_by_user_id`. Any other Eloquent change throws
+`LogicException`. A ticket can be called exactly once: calling marks it
+`called` and records `called_at` + the calling user; calling a non-waiting
+ticket throws `LogicException`, and only members of the ticket's entity may
+call (others get `AuthorizationException`, ticket unchanged).
